k leadership skills.\n\nWe need to weigh. Reliability: C is 100% reliable. Stress resilience: B handles stress well, D responds adequately, A anticipates dangerous situations (maybe proactive). Technical competence: A sees complex connections, spatial vision; B excellent computer skills; D solves problems extremely well; C makes correct decisions quickly.\n\nCooperation: C creates positive atmosphere; B can be uncooperative; D arrogant; A leadership but unorganized.\n\nResponsibility: D takes responsibility seriously; A leadership; B conscientious; C reliable.\n\nOverall, C seems strong on reliability, decision making, crew atmosphere, but has communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education (maybe adaptability). B strong on stress, conscientious, but uncooperative and grumpy. D strong problem solving, responsibility, concentration, but arrogant and weak leadership. A strong anticipation, leadership, but unorganized, poor at criticism.\n\nWhich candidate best overall? Probably C, despite communication issues, but positive crew atmosphere and reliability are crucial. However egocentric and unwilling to further education could be risk. B's uncooperative is concerning for crew. D's arrogance also concerning. A's unorganized and poor at criticism could affect safety.\n\nThus I might recommend Candidate C as provisional, but note concerns.\n\nWe need to state vote in METADATA_JSON.\n\nPublic message: state recommendation, refer to no prior discussion (first turn). Provide evidence: reliability 100%, positive crew atmosphere, quick correct decisions. Mention concerns: communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education, and why still best.\n\nLet's produce."}
